  "text": "Fairy mound is a folkloric motif about haunted hills. A mound at Finnachaid was home to the tragic king Lir. Each year after his leaving, Tara was rebuilt. The hero Finn Mac Cumhaill killed Aillen with a poisoned spear. Its fumes were so foul that no one could sleep, not even those eased by Aillen's music. Another figure, Aillen Trechenn, had three heads. This being struck Tara and Emain Macha in Ulster. It lived in the cave of Oweynagat at Cruachan. The poet Amairgin killed it. The cave usually held the Morrigan, so the being may link to her. A third Aillen, brother of the goddess Aine, loved the spouse of the ocean deity Manannan mac Lir.",
